"Shape: Sigil": {
  "index": "1",
  "category": "sorcery",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Shape: Sigil"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "The sigil shape will create a sigil in the world at the targeted point.  The preparation aspect allows sigils to be cast for far less mana than other shapes for its complexity. The range attribute will change how far away you can place the sigil. The radius attribute will change the size of the sigil's effect when triggered.\n\nThe magnitude effect changes what will trigger the sigil.\nMagnitude 1: Anything\nMagnitude 2: Anything living\nMagnitude 3: Players only.\n\nDamage will always trigger the sigil.\n\nSigils can be made "
        },
        {
          "text": "permanent",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " by casting them on a "
        },
        {
          "text": "metal ritual rune",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". When this is done, the Sigil will gain charges and a cooldown. Charges can be replenished by either "
        },
        {
          "text": "casting additional Sigil spells (contents do not matter)",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " on to an existing sigil, or by "
        },
        {
          "text": "placing them within range of a Mana Pylon (line of sight not required)",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". Permanent Sigils can hold up to "
        },
        {
          "text": "10 charges",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and will go into cooldown mode for "
        },
        {
          "text": "3 seconds",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " once triggered, during which time the sigil will flash. When looking at a Sigil, if you are the caster, you will be shown how many charges it has left. Attacking a sigil will destroy it, and will set it off. \n\nSigils can be permanently made less visible by casting an invisibility spell on them."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "related_recipes": [
    {
      "type": "spell_part",
      "location": "mna:shapes/rune"
    }
  ]
}